Add DPD "don't send our collection address" toggle (v0.108)

Settings > DPD sender address was always sent as the booking's
collectionDetails block, which is what actually determines the address DPD
collect from / return to. Some accounts want DPD's own configured collection
address used instead (e.g. a different pickup point than the registered
address in Settings). DPD's API has no explicit "use account default" flag,
but per the existing comment in DpdShippingService (confirmed when the
collectionDetails nesting fix was originally made), simply not sending the
block at all reliably produces that fallback.

New toggle in Settings > DPD > Sender / collection address: when on,
buildRequestBody() skips putting collectionDetails on the request entirely,
rather than sending it with blank fields. Deliberately does NOT touch
exporterDetails on customs shipments - DPD rejects those outright without a
complete exporter address, so that block stays mandatory and always sent
regardless of this setting.

